-- title:
--   Igusa: the two-chart model of X₀(N) over ℤ_{(ℓ)}
-- statement:
--   Fix an integer $N \neq 0$ and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$. Write $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ for the ring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) and $F$ for the full modular function field `modularFunctionFieldFull N`, and let `chartAlgFin N ℓ` and `chartAlgInf N ℓ` be the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebras `chartAlg N ℓ` of $F$ generated by the $j$-invariant `jFull N` and by its inverse respectively. The scheme [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme N ℓ`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaScheme.html#L255) is the pushout, in schemes, of the two morphisms `fFin N ℓ : XMid N ℓ ⟶ XFin N ℓ` and `fInf N ℓ : XMid N ℓ ⟶ XInf N ℓ` obtained by applying $\operatorname{Spec}$ to the ring inclusions `inclFin N ℓ` and `inclInf N ℓ`, i.e. the gluing of the finite and the infinite $j$-chart along their overlap; the morphism `igusaTo N ℓ` to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ is the one induced on this pushout by the structure morphisms of the two charts. The assertion is the conjunction of three statements about `igusaTo N ℓ`: it is proper, it is smooth of relative dimension $1$, and it is geometrically integral.
--
--   This is Igusa's good-reduction theorem for the modular curve of level $N$ at a prime $\ell$ not dividing $N$, in the form required for the explicit two-chart $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-model used in this development. The three conjuncts are exactly the properties of the structure morphism needed to regard [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme N ℓ`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaScheme.html#L255) as a smooth proper model with integral geometric fibres, and they are consumed by the constructions of curve models and of the Deligne–Rapoport level packages downstream.
